ated across if-else"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/233097670","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/1874#issuecomment-233097670","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/1874","id":233097670,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzMzA5NzY3MA==","user":{"login":"gnprice","id":28173,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4MTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28173?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice","html_url":"https://github.com/gnprice","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-07-16T00:32:33Z","updated_at":"2016-07-16T00:32:33Z","body":"It seems like there are (at least) two or three things that could be done here:\n- We don't allow these, and in many cases it'd be helpful if we did. This is complicated to get right, though. This is covered in existing issues.\n- The error message is confusingly worded, because at runtime the class is never \"already\" defined.\n- The error message isn't specific about where the other definition is -- which, when the code isn't a tiny example program, leaves the user to wonder if the puzzling message is really referring to that other definition up in the `if` or to some other place where it really was \"already\" defined, if they've even spotted the previous definition yet.\n\nI think fixing the last point would in itself mitigate the confusing wording a lot, because it'd be totally explicit what other definition the checker has in mind and the user can figure out that that might be a problem even when they're never duplicated at runtime. So if nothing else, we should add a `previously defined here` note on that error.\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/233097670/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"gnprice","id":28173,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4MTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28173?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice","html_url":"https://github.com/gnprice","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":725033040,"node_id":"MDE1Ok1pbGVzdG9uZWRFdmVudDcyNTAzMzA0MA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/events/725033040","actor":{"login":"gnprice","id":28173,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4MTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28173?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gnprice","html_url":"https://github.com/gnprice","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/use